            "review_title": "Review at Tasty Thai Viet",
            "review_text": "JSTrip_77\nSarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina1194 contributions\n0\nFresh New Vietnamese-Thai Fusion in Tay Ho\nMar 2019 • Couples\nTay Ho already has a lot of cool dining options but this one is pretty special. It's a brand new restaurant in a brand new, growing commercial center. And, it's incredibly easy to find. If you find the D' Le Roi Soleil commercial center - that HUGE new building with the massive white statue on the corner. Behind the escalators, on the first floor, you'll find this new restaurant. \n\nThe staff is all new as is everything in the restaurant. But, they are working very hard. The manager seems to be on site a lot to make sure that the wait staff (who are not fluent in English) are able to communicate properly with the customers. We had pad Thai (with seafood), massaman curry (also seafood) and the chicken/corn soup and tom yom shrimp. Everything was absolutely delicious though I will say that my dishes, the tom yom and the massaman curry were pretty spicy. Next time I go, I'll ask for my dishes to be a bit less spicy. But, that's not a problem with the restaurant. I'm really eager to go back!!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 9, 2019",
